<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Moussa Cisse Paid $2.19m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Cisse is paid <strong>$2.19m</strong> because the veteran minimum is what a club offers a player it has already had on a training camp deal and a two-way, and guarantee dates do the rest of the work.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went undrafted, so no club owed him a guaranteed dollar.</li>
<li>His two-way season paid him <strong>$85k</strong>, which is a few weeks on an NBA roster.</li>
<li>Nothing in this contract was guaranteed on the day he signed it.</li>
<li>This season’s salary became fully guaranteed on October 1, 2026.</li>
<li>Dallas already pays Gafford, Lively, Aldama and Johnson to play near the basket.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has signed three contracts with Dallas and no other club has signed him at all.</p>

